meridian-icon-pack (0.1.1-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Launcher (start-here-kde/-symbolic) now reuses the Compass app's own
    icon instead of Breeze's generic shape -- deliberate branding choice,
    confirmed via live testing on a dev VM.
  * System Settings (preferences-system, systemsettings) now uses a plain
    compass glyph, amber-tinted from Breeze's actions/compass.svg, instead
    of Breeze's settings-gear icon -- same reasoning, also live-tested.
  * debian/copyright updated: Compass's own icon is correctly attributed
    as first-party (not Breeze/LGPL-3.0) despite living under apps/.

 -- TrashPanda2481 <154713431+TrashPanda2481@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 17 Aug 2026 15:00:00 +0000

meridian-icon-pack (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Initial packaging as a real .deb — replaces the git-clone +
    install.sh distribution path with standard dpkg install and
    debhelper-driven icon-cache triggers (dh_icons).

